Desktop Buddies

Credits

Yarrow created Desktop Buddies, and wrote its original engine and web maker.

Yarrow agreed to release Desktop Buddies, including her original engine and web maker, under the MIT licence (2026-11-10).

The original engine, vendored in apps/maker/tests/golden/original/ so the golden traces can be checked against it, is Yarrow's.

The bundled fonts (DynaPuff, Lexend and Nunito) are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each licence text is beside its font, in packages/peel/fonts/ and apps/maker/src/fonts/, and in a release zip, in app/fonts/.

The Rust crates built into desktop-buddies.exe keep their own licences, listed with their texts in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt in each release zip.
